G12_EXECUTION_BASELINE_JSON {"environment": {"cuda_available": true, "cuda_build": "12.8", "gpu": "NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2060", "gpu_total_memory_bytes": 6442123264, "numpy": "2.4.4", "platform": "Windows-10-10.0.19045-SP0", "python": "3.12.12 | packaged by Anaconda, Inc. | (main, Oct 21 2025, 20:05:38) [MSC v.1929 64 bit (AMD64)]", "python_executable": "D:\\miniminiconda\\envs\\liuyan\\python.exe", "scipy": "1.17.1", "torch": "2.10.0+cu128"}, "initial_g12": {"V17_G12_CODEX_RUN.txt": {"sha256": "53dba736d0f10b30f10df7057889b389aff9883c6e5e8f237e79f25836e9b91d", "text": "V17-G12 | Codex科学实验执行指令：固定强后验的欧氏MAE决策与检索排序归因\n======================================================================\n分支：v17-g12-action-ranking-disentanglement\n主程序：fhm_dapp_tim/fhm_dapp/uji_v17_g12_action_ranking.py\n单测：tests/test_uji_v17_g12_action_ranking.py\n冻结科研方案：fhm_dapp_tim/evidence/v17_g12_action_ranking/DESIGN_V17_G12.md\n\n【第一性原理与已有结果，不要重复发明】\nG8 Anchor T=.6五成员强基线，TUJI/UTS/Tampere CONFIRM\nMAE分别2.657774m、5.107529m、5.987721m。\nG10仅在原主导位置已经合理时提供小幅收益，错误主导模式容易进一步恶化。\nG11中UTS存在16个“RSS 1NN正确邻域而V17 Top1错误邻域”的站点，\n但V17整体比RSS KNN更稳健。Tampere RSS 5NN胜出0.224m\n实际上由两个极端位置的大幅改善驱动。\n需将“空间假设排序错误”与“后验给定时的欧氏点决策规则错误”严格拆开。\n尤其不要忽略：G5此前已经在未锐化Tampere V17上做过\n分量几何中位数和连续Student-t几何中位数；这些算法不是新发明，\nG5未达到统计晋级条件。G12是对更强T=.6后验在三个域的新增控制实验。\n\n【G12干预A：概率分布完全固定，只改点决策】\n原原子后验E5/L192/K192/alpha1，Student-t df4，\n原所有960连续位置中心/尺度，成员/锚点概率身份全部固定。\n用原G8 hierarchical_laws(...)[anchor]生成Anchor T=.6后验。\n三种决策固定如下：\n(1) 原完整分布加权均值（必须逐位置100%数值复现G8）；\n(2) 原G5 weighted_component_geometric_median，最多64迭代，\n    tol1e-5m：此算法忽略连续Student-t尺度，属于中心点离散代理；\n(3) 原V9 spatial_median_from_draws，来自相同冻结Student-t\n    后验的独立128+128随机抽样，seed19801，最多64迭代，tol1e-5m。\n    这是蒙特卡洛近似，不是解析解。\n额外用与决策采样完全独立的seed19802、128+128 Student-t抽样\n评估三种决策在**预测模型自己**的欧氏期望风险（不是实际位置MAE）。\n真实逐位置二维MAE用CAL/CONFIRM物理坐标做事后评分。\n同一个完整后验的Energy Score对三种决策完全相同：\n只需用G8原seed19602、64+64的Student-t连续ES计一次，\n不能说median改善了ES（后验完全没变）。\n绝不使用真实位置、真实楼层、以前结果来选择中位数迭代、采样量、\n是否启用某一动作、权重或任何阈值。\n\n【G12干预B：固定原网络，把空间检索的运算阶段独立展开】\n在全体原FIT锚点的同一个全局anchor id上计算6个打分地图：\n1. prototype_only：softmax(-beta_p * 原FIT RSS原型距离)\n2. neural_only：各E5成员softmax(beta_n * 原神经检索logit)后取均值\n3. fused_equal_members：原神经+原型融合后，各成员完整先验等权平均\n4. fused_radial_members：完整先验按R3原Top-L径向方差权重合并\n5. topL_radial_members：R3成员Top-L归一化后散射到全FIT锚点再径向加权\n6. R3_consensus_K192：原R3 alpha1的Top-K共识锚点概率，其他anchor为0\n注意prototype_only和neural_only是两个平行视角，\n不是时间上串行的检索步骤，不能无脑用转移次数声称因果。\n零参模型，不改变原任何R3算子，不从这6个视角挑最优预测算法。\n真实目标building/floor/xy绝不输入6个地图；它们仅在地图预测完成后\n用于10m同建筑同楼层Top1命中、近邻概率质量、\n最近真值邻域anchor排名及各阶段配对转换的事后诊断。\nT=.6锐化不改变anchor Top1 ID，必须在代码内检查。\n\n【数据/科学身份约束】\n原TUJI CAL+CONFIRM、UTS CAL+CONFIRM、Tampere CONFIRM；\n总计909物理站点、4825扫描，只有各自原TRAIN-internal角色。\n只加载原15份冻结E5 checkpoint，原G4/G5/G6角色边界，\nFIT字典与坐标原点保持原样。原始外部/test/outer/官方验证不能打开。\n任何CAL/CONFIRM标签只能参与评估与事后诊断，不能参与预测/模型选择。\n这5个历史角色早已G4-G11反复观察；结果只能是回顾性机制实验，\n不得“通过检验”就宣称新盲测、方法可发表或概率校准成立。\n每物理位置先聚合其多个扫描的误差，再对位置等权求macro MAE。\n保存完整物理坐标keys、逐站点预测误差、模型预期风险、\n后验ES、行动位置移动量、6阶段近邻命中/质量/排序、转移计数。\n必须检查p90/p95、最差位置、尾部风险，不能只看宏平均。\n\n【严格执行顺序：准备前可修G12合成测试bug】\n仓库根目录，在原 liuyan/CUDA 环境运行：\npython -m compileall -q fhm_dapp_tim/fhm_dapp/uji_v17_g12_action_ranking.py tests/test_uji_v17_g12_action_ranking.py\npython -m pytest -q tests/test_uji_v17_g12_action_ranking.py tests/test_uji_v17_g11_rss_identifiability.py tests/test_uji_v17_g10_evidence_corrected_law.py tests/test_uji_v17_g9_anchor_support_diagnostic.py tests/test_uji_v17_g8_hierarchical_attribution.py\npython -m fhm_dapp_tim.fhm_dapp.uji_v17_g12_action_ranking preflight\n\n全部通过后冻结科研方案与源码：\npython -m fhm_dapp_tim.fhm_dapp.uji_v17_g12_action_ranking prepare\npython -m fhm_dapp_tim.fhm_dapp.uji_v17_g12_action_ranking check\n\n仅一次正式GPU评分（不训练）：\npython -m fhm_dapp_tim.fhm_dapp.uji_v17_g12_action_ranking run --device cuda\npython -m fhm_dapp_tim.fhm_dapp.uji_v17_g12_action_ranking check\n\nprepare前发现真实bug可以只在新增G12源码/单测中最小修复，记录\n故障原因与回归测试；绝不修改G1-G11历史科学源码或方法常数凑指标。\n正式run之前写不可变.lock；一旦锁写入，即使发生错误也必须STOP，\n不得删锁反复尝试、偷偷改seed或观察结果后选算法。\n全部G12预测冻结之后，才读取旧G8/G11结果核对：\n原Anchor T=.6五个角色每物理站点MAE/ES应与G8完全一致，\n排序原型Top1与G11相同；若不一致报告不可判定。\n如网络原权重hash不符、原角色分区出错、R3共识不等于joint边缘、\n输出有NaN/Inf、确认数据参与动作优化，立即STOP。\n\n【结果输出（本地再由用户上传GitHub）】\nfhm_dapp_tim/evidence/v17_g12_action_ranking/\n  DESIGN_V17_G12.md\n  manifest_v17_g12.json\n  run_v17_g12.lock\n  diagnosis_v17_g12.json\n  RUN_REPORT_V17_G12.md\n  RUN_NOTES.md（简洁：测试数、GPU/耗时、权重SHA校验、一次正式运行、\n                出现bug的精确修复记录、G1-G11历史文件不变）\n不生成几十份工程审计报告；不上传原始.pt。\n每个域必须给：\n(1) 原均值/分量中位数/连续中位数的绝对MAE、p90/p95/极端尾部；\n(2) 同一后验下模型期望风险与真实误差是否一致变化；\n(3) 六阶段10m命中、近邻质量、排序变化，特别是UTS困难位置；\n(4) 原Tampere(262.94,107.04)与(262.94,112.04)的动作改动与错误。\n禁止根据这轮已暴露确认标签决定新版门控。\n\n【交给ChatGPT后讨论的决策问题】\n若中位数在模型期望风险降低且真实MAE也稳定降低，下一步考虑\n独立验证这条已有决策规则；它本身不是Q1创新。\n若模型期望风险降低但真值MAE变差，要追问后验失配而非乱改median。\n若RSS原型对而fused/neural错造成显著失误，下一步才值得训练\n基于真正新划分的RSS空间困难负样本判别模型。\n如果没有证据能让新模型可靠超越现有强E5，就停止G系列的\n后处理版本，直接进入新数据划分和完整可学习建模。\n任何论文级结论仍需要未观察过的物理位置独立评估和\n原V17 E5/E16/E25相同预算对照、ES与尾部风险。\n\n【Git归属】所有Git checkout、commit、push、上传由用户自己处理。\nCodex不要执行任何Git命令，只做科学测试、一次正式运行、简洁产物。\n"}, "fhm_dapp_tim/evidence/v17_g12_action_ranking/DESIGN_V17_G12.md": {"sha256": "1f7e93fdf94ac383317c62573886f3664c2b27daaef4eb492d89b987a0e7ded5", "text": "# G12 — Frozen Anchor-T=.6 posterior: MAE action vs retrieval-stage ranking\n**Pre-outcome, single retrospective mechanism check, 2026-10-10.**\n\n## Why this question?\n\nG8 anchor-only T=.6 became the strong common E5/L192/K192/alpha1 comparator (TUJI 2.657774m, UTS 5.107529m, Tampere 5.987721m on historical CONFIRM). G9–G11 found (i) wrong dominant spatial modes can yield catastrophic point errors even with near-site candidates present, (ii) raw RSS/learned ranking has complementary corrections, and (iii) Tampere RSS 5NN's 0.224m aggregate gain is entirely due to two disastrous V17 decisions. Before training a new network, isolate *ranking* versus *decision* effects.\n\n**Prior art in this same repo:** G5 already tested weighted component-centre geometric median and sampled continuous Student-t Weiszfeld median on the **untempered Tampere** E5 posterior, 7.202666m mean versus 6.680664m component median and 6.820973m continuous median, with NO internal promotion. The V9 sampler/Weiszfeld implementation is reused exactly. Do not claim this is new or algorithmically novel. G12's nonredundant contribution is the **stronger G8 sharpened anchor posterior on three original data domains** plus stage-by-stage ranking diagnosis, with a pair of independent posterior risk / realized MAE measurements.\n\n## Fixed experiment, no training\n\nUse the exact same old 15 frozen E5 checkpoints, the original G8 R3 member Top-L192, alpha=1 K192 consensus, df4 Student-t component centres and scales, shared Anchor-only T=.6 law. No E16/E25 inference, no official or external test file, no recalibration, no hyperparameter search, no new models, no confirmation fitting, no candidate pruning. All old CAL/CONFIRM data have already been observed many times, so no prospective scientific claim or p-value-based promotion is legitimate.\n\nAction intervention holds *identical* q(m,k), original 960 centres and per-coordinate scales. For each query compare ONLY:\n\n1. Original exact mixture mean (G8/G11 baseline). Floating-point summation remains original E5*K order.\n2. Existing G5 64-iteration weighted component-centre geometric median: Dirac-centre surrogate which deliberately ignores Student-t component spread.\n3. Existing V9 Weiszfeld geometric median from **two independent Student-t sampling streams**, 128 draws per stream, seed 19801. Same Student-t 4df full 960-component distribution, original centres/scales and weights. Approximation not analytic Bayes action.\n\nFixed Weiszfeld tolerance 1e-5m, 64 iterations. The *model-implied* expected Euclidean loss for these three fixed actions is estimated with a **separate independent** two-stream 128+128 Student-t sample seed 19802. Do NOT use realization target Y to choose which action, change number of draws, or stop algorithm early on score. The model-implied risk is NOT the ground truth realized error. All three actions have identical continuous energy score (the predictive law is unchanged); compute it ONCE from original G8 shared MC seed 19602, 64+64 per scan, and verify numeric match with G8 historic original posterior later. Do NOT count shared ES as evidence of one action beating another.\n\nThis separates:\n(a) decision improvement consistent with posterior loss minimization;\n(b) posterior misspecification when risk improvement fails to translate to measured error;\n(c) finite-draw approximation limitations (reported, not tuned).\n\n## Ranking attribution: same original full FIT dictionary\n\nWith NO labels passed into ranking, calculate six well-defined [rows, all FIT anchors] probability maps, independently of the new action:\n\n- prototype_only: softmax(-beta_prototype * original FIT prototype RSS distance).\n- neural_only: mean over E5 individual softmax(beta_neural * original neural retrieval logits).\n- fused_equal_members: arithmetic mean of *actual original* neural+prototype fused full per-member priors, before member Top-L and radial weights.\n- fused_radial_members: original full fused priors, combined using inverse-square of R3 member radial spread estimated from original Top-L.\n- topL_radial_members: original Top-L normalized member probabilities, scattered to all FIT anchors using original radial member weights, prior to alpha consensus epsilon.\n- R3_consensus_K192: original true alpha1 K192 sparse/dense consensus, zero outside the selected K anchors. Anchor T=.6 strictly preserves its Top1 identity.\n\nThese maps are explanatory counterfactual scoring operators. In particular prototype_only and neural_only are **alternative inputs**, not literal serial transformations. The fused_equal_members to fused_radial_members step isolates actual member confidence reweighting, while radial to Top-L and Top-L to consensus compare truncation/support effects. Because Top-L is renormalized and consensus adds epsilon and Top-K truncation, these stages need not yield identical rankings even at alpha1. Do not present the above maps as independently calibrated posteriors.\n\nUsing the query true XY/building/floor only AFTER all predictions, compute 10m same-building+floor Top1 hit, probability mass and first eligible anchor rank for every map; undefined rank if no physically near FIT anchor. Report site-macro summaries and site vectors. Report label-facing consecutive transition counts (right-to-wrong, wrong-to-right). This is not a deployable gate; do not build a rule selecting the best stage by comparing to true site.\n\n## Data, reporting and interpretation\n\nFive original TRAIN-internal historical roles:\nTUJI CAL+CONFIRM, UTS CAL+CONFIRM, Tampere CONFIRM. No original FIT-label-driven new training. Compute row actions with fixed draws and then average row errors at each physical coordinate, then average sites. Save each physical-site key and complete paired vectors for mean, component median, continuous median, model-implied risk, action displacement and six-stage ranking. Report macro MAE, median/p90/p95/max and severe tail (>=10m/20m). ES for shared posterior only. Include matched comparison to the G8 exact mean MAE/ES across all five roles **after G12 lock/result freeze**, never in G12 decision code.\n\nDecision for subsequent stage:\n- If continuous median markedly improves both absolute MAE and severe tails across domains, its fixed-Bayes-action benefit merits *independent prospective* confirmation; it is not a novel theoretical contribution and cannot independently substantiate Q1.\n- If model-implied risk falls but physical error does not, evidence shifts toward posterior *misidentification*, not point-action optimization.\n- If prototype is correct/neural wrong and fused loses correct anchors in UTS hard sites, prioritise a learned spatial discriminative likelihood/representation, not another T grid. If neural-only helps compensate raw RSS catastrophic mistakes, preserve its benefit.\n- If the learned consensus is often correct top1 but the mixture mean is far, distinguish wrong spatial mode concentration from mismatched point decision.\n- If neither probe materially changes future design, stop the cheap G-series retrospectives: next training step needs a genuinely fresh, physically isolated development split and equal-budget E5/E16/E25, full continuous proper scores.\n\n**JCR Q1 boundary:** The posterior, action method and ranking diagnostics here are existing tools. This iteration exists to falsify a modelling assumption, not to present an incremental algorithm as publishable invention.\n"}, "fhm_dapp_tim/fhm_dapp/uji_v17_g12_action_ranking.py": {"sha256": "d3ad96e17e9d47841f403ae8bcca6595851b9509e41a9444cace69e67c88912c", "text": "\"\"\"G12: disentangle V17 spatial ranking from Euclidean-MAE point action.\n\nZero new training / no model selection. G5 already tried medians on the\nuntempered Tampere posterior; G12 tests the *stronger frozen G8 anchor-T=.6*\nlaw across TUJI/UTS/Tampere, while decomposing retrieval stages within the\nsame original E5 networks. Continuous geometric median is the existing\nV9 Weiszfeld approximation, with action draws independent from risk and ES.\n\nHistorical CAL/CONFIRM outcomes are all exposed. These are retrospective\ndescriptive scientific mechanisms, NOT blind estimates or Q1 promotion.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Sequence\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport torch\n\nfrom fhm_dapp_tim.fhm_dapp import uji_v17_g8_hierarchical_attribution as g8\nfrom fhm_dapp_tim.fhm_dapp import uji_v17_g5_bayes_action as g5\nfrom fhm_dapp_tim.fhm_dapp import uji_v17_mother_r2b as r2b\nfrom fhm_dapp_tim.fhm_dapp import uji_v17_mother_r3 as r3\nfrom fhm_dapp_tim.fhm_dapp import uji_v17_mother_r3_protocol as r3p\nfrom fhm_dapp_tim.fhm_dapp.coherent_marked_v9 import (\n    common_student_t_randomness, sample_continuous_mixture,\n    spatial_median_from_draws,\n)\nfrom fhm_dapp_tim.fhm_dapp.experiment_v7 import (\n    _canonical_json_sha256, _sha256_file, _write_json_new,\n)\n\nROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nEVIDENCE=ROOT/\"evidence/v17_g12_action_ranking\"\nDESIGN=EVIDENCE/\"DESIGN_V17_G12.md\"\nMANIFEST=EVIDENCE/\"manifest_v17_g12.json\"\nLOCK=EVIDENCE/\"run_v17_g12.lock\"\nRESULT=EVIDENCE/\"diagnosis_v17_g12.json\"\nREPORT=EVIDENCE/\"RUN_REPORT_V17_G12.md\"\nPROTOCOL=\"v17_g12_frozen_anchor_action_and_rank_chain_20261010\"\nDOMAINS=(\"tuji\",\"uts\",\"tampere\")\nROLES=g8.ROLES\nE,L,K=5,192,192\nBATCH=16\nRADIUS=10.0\nTEMPERATURE=0.6\nACTION_SEED=19801\nRISK_SEED=19802\nACTION_DRAWS=128\nRISK_DRAWS=128\nMEDIAN_ITERATIONS=64\nMEDIAN_TOL=1e-5\nACTIONS=(\"mean\",\"component_median\",\"continuous_median\")\nSTAGES=(\"prototype_only\",\"neural_only\",\"fused_equal_members\",\n        \"fused_radial_members\",\"topL_radial_members\",\"R3_consensus_K192\")\nDIAGNOSTICS=(\"site_near_mass\",\"site_top1_in10m\",\"site_best_near_rank\")\nPREDICTIVE_ES_SEED=g8.SEED\n\n\nclass G12Error(RuntimeError):\n    pass\n\n\ndef _write(path:Path,object:dict,field:str=\"result_sha256\")->dict:\n    if path.exists():\n        raise FileExistsError(f\"G12 immutable file already exists: {path}\")\n    value=dict(object)\n    value[field]=_canonical_json_sha256(value)\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\n    _write_json_new(path,value)\n    return value\n\n\ndef _read(path:Path,field:str=\"result_sha256\")->dict:\n    record=json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    if record.get(field)!=_canonical_json_sha256(record,omit=field):\n        raise G12Error(f\"G12 evidence hash changed: {path}\")\n    return record\n\n\ndef _source_hashes()->dict:\n    files={\n        \"design\":DESIGN,\"g12\":Path(__file__),\n        \"tests\":ROOT.parent/\"tests/test_uji_v17_g12_action_ranking.py\",\n        \"g8\":Path(g8.__file__),\"g5\":Path(g5.__file__),\n        \"r2b\":Path(r2b.__file__),\"r3\":Path(r3.__file__),\n        \"r3_protocol\":Path(r3p.__file__),\n        \"sampler\":Path(sample_continuous_mixture.__code__.co_filename),\n    }\n    return {key:_sha256_file(path) for key,path in files.items()}\n\n\ndef preflight()->dict:\n    if (g8.E!=E or g8.K!=K or g8.g6.L!=L or g8.g6.ALPHA!=1.0\n        or g8.T!=TEMPERATURE or r3p.STUDENT_DF!=4.0\n        or r3p.PREDICTIVE_DRAWS_PER_STREAM!=64):\n        raise G12Error(\"frozen G8 E5/L192/K192/alpha1/T.6/Student-t changed\")\n    sources={domain:g8._pack(domain)[\"original\"] for domain in DOMAINS}\n    return {\"status\":\"FROZEN_E5_RANK_AND_ACTION_READY\",\n            \"protocol\":PROTOCOL,\n            \"source_sha256\":_source_hashes(),\n            \"model_and_role_provenance\":sources,\n            \"no_training\":True,\"no_official_or_provided_test\":True,\n            \"historical_label_exposure\":True}\n\n\ndef prepare()->dict:\n    checked=preflight()\n    manifest={\n        \"protocol\":PROTOCOL,\"source_sha256\":checked[\"source_sha256\"],\n        \"model_and_role_provenance\":checked[\"model_and_role_provenance\"],\n        \"roles\":{d:list(ROLES[d]) for d in DOMAINS},\n        \"actions\":list(ACTIONS),\"ranking_stages\":list(STAGES),\n        \"batch\":BATCH,\"E\":E,\"L\":L,\"K\":K,\"alpha\":1.0,\n        \"anchor_temperature\":TEMPERATURE,\"student_df\":4.0,\n        \"ranking_hit_radius_m\":RADIUS,\n        \"action_seed\":ACTION_SEED,\"risk_seed\":RISK_SEED,\n        \"action_draws_per_stream\":ACTION_DRAWS,\n        \"risk_draws_per_stream\":RISK_DRAWS,\n        \"median_iterations\":MEDIAN_ITERATIONS,\n        \"median_tolerance_m\":MEDIAN_TOL,\n        \"energy_seed\":PREDICTIVE_ES_SEED,\n        \"energy_draws_per_stream\":r3p.PREDICTIVE_DRAWS_PER_STREAM,\n        \"shared_energy_for_all_actions\":True,\n        \"diagnostics_posthoc_only\":True,\"no_truth_gating\":True,\n        \"all_train_internal_confirmations_previously_seen\":True,\n        \"no_new_model_fit_or_hyperparameter_selection\":True,\n    }\n    manifest[\"manifest_sha256\"]=_canonical_json_sha256(manifest)\n    if MANIFEST.exists():\n        if _read(MANIFEST,\"manifest_sha256\")!=manifest:\n            raise G12Error(\"G12 frozen plan/source mismatch\")\n        return manifest\n    _write_json_new(MANIFEST,manifest)\n    return manifest\n\n\ndef _draws_for_batch(records:dict,start:int,end:int,device:torch.device)->dict:\n    return {key:(value[start:end].to(device)\n                 if isinstance(value,torch.Tensor) and value.ndim>0 else value)\n            for key,value in records.items()}\n\n\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef actions_from_frozen_law(\n    joint:torch.Tensor,xy:torch.Tensor,sigma:torch.Tensor,\n    action_draws:dict\n)->dict[str,torch.Tensor]:\n    \"\"\"Same posterior, three point decisions. No label is an argument.\"\"\"\n    if (joint.ndim!=2 or joint.shape[1]!=E*K\n        or xy.shape!=(*joint.shape,2) or sigma.shape!=xy.shape\n        or not torch.isfinite(joint).all()\n        or not torch.isfinite(xy).all() or not torch.isfinite(sigma).all()\n        or (sigma<=0).any() or (joint<0).any()):\n        raise G12Error(\"invalid frozen mixture law\")\n    if not torch.allclose(joint.sum(dim=1),torch.ones(len(joint),device=joint.device),\n                          atol=4e-6,rtol=4e-6):\n        raise G12Error(\"posterior not normalized\")\n    # Preserve G8 exact float32 summation of E*K mean locations.\n    mean=(joint[:,:,None]*xy).sum(1)\n    component=g5.weighted_component_geometric_median(\n        joint,xy,iterations=MEDIAN_ITERATIONS,tolerance=MEDIAN_TOL)\n    first=sample_continuous_mixture(\n        joint,xy,sigma,action_draws[\"uniform_1\"],action_draws[\"noise_1\"])\n    second=sample_continuous_mixture(\n        joint,xy,sigma,action_draws[\"uniform_2\"],action_draws[\"noise_2\"])\n    continuous=spatial_median_from_draws(\n        first,second,maximum_iterations=MEDIAN_ITERATIONS,tolerance=MEDIAN_TOL)\n    if (not torch.isfinite(component).all() or\n        not torch.isfinite(continuous).all()):\n        raise G12Error(\"nonfinite frozen-law point decisions\")\n    return {\"mean\":mean,\"component_median\":component,\n            \"continuous_median\":continuous}\n\n\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef predicted_point_risk(\n    actions:dict[str,torch.Tensor],joint:torch.Tensor,\n    xy:torch.Tensor,sigma:torch.Tensor,risk_draws:dict\n)->dict[str,torch.Tensor]:\n    \"\"\"Independent MC estimate of expected Euclidean loss UNDER THE MODEL.\n\n    NOT the true location risk. No query label. If median risk improves but\n    measured MAE worsens, posterior mismatch is a plausible explanation.\n    \"\"\"\n    f=sample_continuous_mixture(\n        joint,xy,sigma,risk_draws[\"uniform_1\"],risk_draws[\"noise_1\"])\n    s=sample_continuous_mixture(\n        joint,xy,sigma,risk_draws[\"uniform_2\"],risk_draws[\"noise_2\"])\n    return {name:.5*(torch.linalg.vector_norm(\n                f.double()-a[:,None,:].double(),dim=-1).mean(1)+\n                torch.linalg.vector_norm(\n                s.double()-a[:,None,:].double(),dim=-1).mean(1))\n            for name,a in actions.items()}\n\n\ndef ranking_probability_panels(\n    distance:torch.Tensor,neural_logits:torch.Tensor,\n    full_prior:torch.Tensor,top_prob:torch.Tensor,top_ids:torch.Tensor,\n    radial:torch.Tensor,consensus_ids:torch.Tensor,\n    consensus_prior:torch.Tensor\n)->dict[str,torch.Tensor]:\n    \"\"\"Label-free aligned [B,A] stage maps; not modified V17 decisions.\n\n    STAGES are mechanism counterfactual ranking maps:\n    original prototype similarity; neural-only member mean;\n    mixed fused posterior with equal and radial member weight;\n    truncated Top-L radial-weight pool; actual R3 consensus Top-K.\n    Neural-only vs prototype-only are ALTERNATIVES not temporal steps.\n    \"\"\"\n    e,b,a=neural_logits.shape\n    if (e!=E or distance.shape!=(b,a)\n        or full_prior.shape!=(E,b,a)\n        or top_prob.shape!=(E,b,L)\n        or top_ids.shape!=(E,b,L)\n        or radial.shape!=(E,b)\n        or consensus_ids.shape!=(b,K)\n        or consensus_prior.shape!=(b,K)):\n        raise G12Error(\"mismatched full retrieval and R3 consensus dimensions\")\n    if ((top_ids<0).any() or (top_ids>=a).any()\n        or (consensus_ids<0).any() or (consensus_ids>=a).any()):\n        raise G12Error(\"invalid global FIT anchor IDs\")\n    wm=radial.square().clamp_min(1e-8).reciprocal()\n    wm=wm/wm.sum(0,keepdim=True).clamp_min(1e-30)\n    proto=torch.softmax(-r3p.BETA_PROTOTYPE*distance,dim=1)\n    neural=torch.softmax(r3p.BETA_NEURAL*neural_logits,dim=2).mean(0)\n    equal=full_prior.mean(0)\n    radial_full=(wm[:,:,None]*full_prior).sum(0)\n    sparse=torch.zeros_like(equal)\n    sparse.scatter_add_(1,top_ids.permute(1,0,2).reshape(b,E*L),\n                        (wm[:,:,None]*top_prob).permute(1,0,2).reshape(b,E*L))\n    sparse=sparse/sparse.sum(1,keepdim=True).clamp_min(1e-30)\n    consensus=torch.zeros_like(equal)\n    consensus.scatter_(1,consensus_ids,consensus_prior)\n    maps=dict(zip(STAGES,(proto,neural,equal,radial_full,sparse,consensus)))\n    for name,prob in maps.items():\n        if not torch.isfinite(prob).all() or (prob<0).any() or not torch.allclose(\n            prob.sum(1),torch.ones(b,device=prob.device),atol=5e-6,rtol=5e-6):\n            raise G12Error(f\"invalid stage posterior {name}\")\n    return maps\n\n\ndef ranking_label_diagnostics(\n    panels:dict[str,torch.Tensor],\n    anchor_xy:torch.Tensor,anchor_build:torch.Tensor,\n    anchor_floor:torch.Tensor,true_xy:torch.Tensor,\n    true_build:torch.Tensor,true_floor:torch.Tensor\n)->dict[str,torch.Tensor]:\n    \"\"\"Retrospective labels only; NEVER passed into any inference path.\"\"\"\n    b,a=true_xy.shape[0],anchor_xy.shape[0]\n    near=(torch.cdist(true_xy,anchor_xy)<=RADIUS+1e-5)\n    near &= (anchor_build[None,:]==true_build[:,None])\n    near &= (anchor_floor[None,:]==true_floor[:,None])\n    out={\"near_reference_exists\":near.any(1).float()}\n    for name,prob in panels.items():\n        if prob.shape!=(b,a):\n            raise G12Error(f\"wrong stage shape: {name}\")\n        order=torch.argsort(prob,dim=1,stable=True,descending=True)\n        top=order[:,0]\n        near_sorted=near.gather(1,order)\n        first=torch.where(near_sorted,torch.arange(\n            1,a+1,device=near.device)[None,:].expand(b,-1),\n            torch.full_like(order,a+1)).min(1).values\n        out[name+\"_top1_in10m\"]=near.gather(1,top[:,None]).squeeze(1).float()\n        out[name+\"_near10_mass\"]=(prob*near).sum(1)\n        out[name+\"_best_near_rank\"]=torch.where(\n            first<=a,first.double(),\n            torch.full((b,),float(\"nan\"),device=near.device,dtype=torch.float64))\n    return out\n\n\ndef _site_vector(row:torch.Tensor,gid:torch.Tensor,sites:int)->list:\n    x=row.detach().cpu().double()\n    g=gid.detach().cpu().long()\n    mask=torch.isfinite(x)\n    sum_=torch.zeros(sites,dtype=torch.float64)\n    count=torch.zeros(sites,dtype=torch.float64)\n    sum_.scatter_add_(0,g,torch.where(mask,x,torch.zeros_like(x)))\n    count.scatter_add_(0,g,mask.double())\n    return [float(a/b) if b else None for a,b in\n            zip(sum_.tolist(),count.tolist())]\n\n\ndef _summary(vectors:dict[str,list])->dict:\n    out={}\n    for name,values in vectors.items():\n        x=np.asarray([v for v in values if v is not None],dtype=np.float64)\n        out[name]={\"site_mean\":float(x.mean()) if len(x) else None,\n                   \"n_finite_sites\":len(x),\"n_sites\":len(values)}\n        if name.endswith(\"_mae_m\") and len(x):\n            sorted_desc=np.sort(x)[::-1]\n            out[name].update({\n                \"median_m\":float(np.median(x)),\n                \"p90_m\":float(np.quantile(x,.9)),\n                \"p95_m\":float(np.quantile(x,.95)),\n                \"p99_m\":float(np.quantile(x,.99)),\n                \"worst_5pct_mean_m\":float(sorted_desc[:max(1,int(np.ceil(.05*len(x))))].mean()),\n                \"sites_ge_10m\":int((x>=10).sum()),\n                \"sites_ge_20m\":int((x>=20).sum()),\n                \"max_m\":float(np.max(x))})\n    return out\n\n\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef score_role(models:list,data:dict,rows:np.ndarray,origin:np.ndarray)->dict:\n    ref=models[0]\n    device=next(ref.parameters()).device\n    n=len(rows)\n    gid,ordered=r2b._coordinate_groups([data[\"keys\"][int(i)] for i in rows])\n    target=torch.as_tensor(data[\"raw_xy\"][rows]-origin[None,:],\n                           dtype=torch.float64,device=device)\n    truth_b=torch.as_tensor(data[\"building\"][rows],dtype=torch.long,device=device)\n    truth_f=torch.as_tensor(data[\"floor\"][rows],dtype=torch.long,device=device)\n    a=int(ref.n_anchors)\n    if a<K:raise G12Error(\"FIT anchors fewer than Top-K192\")\n    anchor_xy=ref.anchor_coords.to(device).float()\n    anchor_build=ref.anchor_buildings.to(device).long()\n    anchor_floor=ref.anchor_floors.to(device).long()\n    action_rng=common_student_t_randomness(n,draws=ACTION_DRAWS,\n                      degrees_freedom=r3p.STUDENT_DF,seed=ACTION_SEED)\n    risk_rng=common_student_t_randomness(n,draws=RISK_DRAWS,\n                      degrees_freedom=r3p.STUDENT_DF,seed=RISK_SEED)\n    es_rng=common_student_t_randomness(n,\n                      draws=r3p.PREDICTIVE_DRAWS_PER_STREAM,\n                      degrees_freedom=r3p.STUDENT_DF,seed=PREDICTIVE_ES_SEED)\n    output:dict[str,torch.Tensor]={}\n    with r3.r2f_a1._deterministic_algorithms():\n        for start in range(0,n,BATCH):\n            end=min(start+BATCH,n)\n            b=end-start\n            rss=data[\"rss\"][rows[start:end]].float().to(device)\n            proto=r2b._prototype_distance(ref,rss)\n            all_ids=torch.arange(a,device=device)[None,:].expand(b,-1)\n            logits=[];loc=[];scales=[]\n            for model in models:\n                enc=model.encoder(rss)\n                logits.append(model.retrieval_logits_from_embedding(enc))\n                x,s=model._components(enc,all_ids)\n                loc.append(x);scales.append(s)\n            logit=torch.stack(logits)\n            full_prior=torch.softmax(\n                r3p.BETA_NEURAL*logit-r3p.BETA_PROTOTYPE*proto[None,:,:],\n                dim=2)\n            top,ix,rad,_=r3._member_top_l(\n                full_prior,torch.stack(loc),torch.stack(scales),\n                L,student_df=r3p.STUDENT_DF)\n            joint,xy,sigma=r3._dense_joint_law(\n                top,ix,rad,torch.stack(loc),torch.stack(scales),\n                tuple(range(E)),top_k=K,alpha=g8.g6.ALPHA)\n            w=rad.square().clamp_min(1e-8).reciprocal()\n            w=w/w.sum(0,keepdim=True).clamp_min(1e-30)\n            ids,c=r3.dense_alpha_consensus_prior(\n                top,ix,w,a,K,epsilon=r3.CONSENSUS_EPSILON,\n                alpha=g8.g6.ALPHA)\n            if not torch.allclose(c,joint.reshape(b,E,K).sum(1),\n                                  atol=3e-6,rtol=3e-6):\n                raise G12Error(\"R3 exact K192 anchor marginal changed\")\n            q=g8.hierarchical_laws(joint,E,K)[\"anchor\"]\n            dec=actions_from_frozen_law(q,xy,sigma,\n                _draws_for_batch(action_rng,start,end,device))\n            risk=predicted_point_risk(dec,q,xy,sigma,\n                _draws_for_batch(risk_rng,start,end,device))\n            # ES and posterior are IDENTICAL for all decisions.\n            es,old_mean=r3._score_joint_law(\n                q,xy,sigma,target[start:end],\n                _draws_for_batch(es_rng,start,end,device))\n            if not torch.allclose(\n                old_mean,torch.linalg.vector_norm(\n                    dec[\"mean\"].double()-target[start:end],dim=1).cpu(),\n                    atol=1e-6,rtol=1e-6):\n                raise G12Error(\"G8 original mean/MAE reconstruction changed\")\n            measures={\"shared_student_t_es_m\":es.to(device),\n                      \"action_shift_component_m\":torch.linalg.vector_norm(\n                          dec[\"component_median\"]-dec[\"mean\"],dim=1),\n                      \"action_shift_continuous_m\":torch.linalg.vector_norm(\n                          dec[\"continuous_median\"]-dec[\"mean\"],dim=1)}\n            for name,xy_dec in dec.items():\n                measures[name+\"_mae_m\"]=torch.linalg.vector_norm(\n                    xy_dec.double()-target[start:end],dim=1)\n                measures[name+\"_model_risk_m\"]=risk[name]\n            panels=ranking_probability_panels(\n                proto,logit,full_prior,top,ix,rad,ids,c)\n            # The sharpened anchor marginal is rank preserving.\n            original_top=panels[\"R3_consensus_K192\"].argmax(1)\n            sharpened=c.pow(1/TEMPERATURE).argmax(1)\n            if not torch.equal(original_top,ids.gather(1,sharpened[:,None]).squeeze(1)):\n                raise G12Error(\"Anchor T0.6 changed anchor Top-1 identity\")\n            diagnostics=ranking_label_diagnostics(\n                panels,anchor_xy,anchor_build,anchor_floor,\n                target[start:end].float(),truth_b[start:end],truth_f[start:end])\n            measures.update(diagnostics)\n            for name,value in measures.items():\n                if name not in output:\n                    output[name]=torch.empty(n,dtype=torch.float64)\n                output[name][start:end]=value.detach().cpu().double()\n    site={name:_site_vector(values,gid,len(ordered)) for name,values in output.items()}\n    stats=_summary(site)\n    delta={k:[a-b for a,b in zip(site[k+\"_mae_m\"],site[\"mean_mae_m\"])]\n           for k in (\"component_median\",\"continuous_median\")}\n    pairs={}\n    for name,ds in delta.items():\n        pairs[name+\"_minus_mean\"]={\n            \"mean_delta_mae_m\":float(np.mean(ds)),\n            \"improved_sites\":sum(x<0 for x in ds),\n            \"worsened_sites\":sum(x>0 for x in ds),\n            \"worst_harm_m\":max(ds),\n            \"best_gain_m\":-min(ds),\n            \"coordinate_vector_delta_mae_m\":ds,\n        }\n    risk_error_alignment={}\n    for name in (\"component_median\",\"continuous_median\"):\n        actual=np.asarray(delta[name],dtype=np.float64)\n        risk_delta=np.asarray(site[name+\"_model_risk_m\"],dtype=np.float64) - (\n            np.asarray(site[\"mean_model_risk_m\"],dtype=np.float64))\n        risk_error_alignment[name]={\n            \"mean_model_risk_delta_m\":float(risk_delta.mean()),\n            \"mean_realized_mae_delta_m\":float(actual.mean()),\n            \"model_risk_improved_sites\":int((risk_delta<0).sum()),\n            \"model_risk_improved_but_real_mae_worse_sites\":\n                int(((risk_delta<0)&(actual>0)).sum()),\n            \"model_risk_worse_but_real_mae_better_sites\":\n                int(((risk_delta>0)&(actual<0)).sum()),\n            \"model_risk_delta_by_site_m\":risk_delta.tolist(),\n        }\n    # Descriptive stage rescue/loss uses true labels; no runtime gate.\n    movements={}\n    for before,after in zip(STAGES[:-1],STAGES[1:]):\n        old=site[before+\"_top1_in10m\"]\n        new=site[after+\"_top1_in10m\"]\n        movements[before+\"__to__\"+after]={\n            \"both_correct\":sum(a>=.5 and b>=.5 for a,b in zip(old,new)),\n            \"lost_correct\":sum(a>=.5 and b<.5 for a,b in zip(old,new)),\n            \"rescued_correct\":sum(a<.5 and b>=.5 for a,b in zip(old,new)),\n            \"both_wrong\":sum(a<.5 and b<.5 for a,b in zip(old,new)),\n        }\n    return {\"rows\":n,\"physical_sites\":len(ordered),\n            \"physical_coordinate_keys\":[list(x) for x in ordered],\n            \"summary\":stats,\"site_vectors\":site,\n            \"decision_effects\":pairs,\n            \"risk_vs_realized_error_posthoc\":risk_error_alignment,\n            \"ranking_stage_transitions_posthoc\":movements,\n            \"oracle_labels_only_for_scoring_diagnostics\":True,\n            \"random_streams_independent\":True}\n\n\ndef _report(record:dict)->str:\n    lines=[\"# G12 | Frozen posterior: ranking vs MAE point decision\",\"\",\n           \"**Retrospective G8 anchor-only T=.6 across original five TRAIN-internal roles.**\",\n           \"G5 already used geometric medians on untempered Tampere;\",\n           \"G12 does not claim a novel median algorithm.\",\"\",\n           \"| Domain / role | Mean MAE m | Discrete centre median m | \"\n           \"Continuous t-median m | ES (all decisions) m |\",\n           \"|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\"]\n    for domain in DOMAINS:\n        for role,x in record[\"by_domain\"][domain].items():\n            s=x[\"summary\"]\n            lines.append(f\"| {domain}/{role} | {s['mean_mae_m']['site_mean']:.6f} | \"\n                f\"{s['component_median_mae_m']['site_mean']:.6f} | \"\n                f\"{s['continuous_median_mae_m']['site_mean']:.6f} | \"\n                f\"{s['shared_student_t_es_m']['site_mean']:.6f} |\")\n    lines.extend([\"\",\"## Ranking stage: coordinate-site macro Top1@10m\",\"\"])\n    for domain in DOMAINS:\n        for role,x in record[\"by_domain\"][domain].items():\n            s=x[\"summary\"]\n            stage_string=\", \".join(\n                f\"{stage}={s[stage+'_top1_in10m']['site_mean']:.4f}\"\n                for stage in STAGES)\n            lines.append(f\"- {domain}/{role}: {stage_string}\")\n            p=x[\"decision_effects\"]\n            lines.append(\n                f\"  Decision ΔMAE vs mean: component \"\n                f\"{p['component_median_minus_mean']['mean_delta_mae_m']:+.6f}m; \"\n                f\"continuous {p['continuous_median_minus_mean']['mean_delta_mae_m']:+.6f}m\")\n            z=x[\"risk_vs_realized_error_posthoc\"][\"continuous_median\"]\n            lines.append(f\"  Continuous median model-risk Δ \"\n                f\"{z['mean_model_risk_delta_m']:+.6f}m; \"\n                f\"risk better / real MAE worse on \"\n                f\"{z['model_risk_improved_but_real_mae_worse_sites']} sites\")\n    lines.extend([\"\",\"## Scientific interpretation boundaries\",\"\",\n        \"- Point actions share EXACTLY one frozen 960-component posterior.\",\n        \"- The training-free continuous median is approximate: 2x128 fixed\",\n        \"  Student-t draws, Weiszfeld 64 iterations, independent MC risk\",\n        \"  sample and the original common-random-numbers ES stream.\",\n        \"- Predicted model risk is NOT the realized Euclidean position MAE.\",\n        \"- Median may lower its own posterior expected risk while worsening\",\n        \"  actual positional error if the posterior is misspecified.\",\n        \"- Prototype/neural-only stage probabilities are analytical\",\n        \"  counterfactuals, not stages of a deployed cascaded predictor.\",\n        \"- Near10m/true-floor labels are only posthoc scientific diagnosis.\",\n        \"- Historical CAL/CONFIRM outcomes have ALREADY been observed;\",\n        \"  no new blind testing, significance-based promotion or Q1 claim.\",\"\",\n        f\"Self hash: {record['result_sha256']}\",\"\"])\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n\ndef run(device_name:str=\"cuda\")->dict:\n    if LOCK.exists() or RESULT.exists():\n        raise G12Error(\"formal experiment already attempted: no rerun\")\n    manifest=prepare()\n    locked=_write(LOCK,{\n        \"protocol\":PROTOCOL,\n        \"manifest_file_sha256\":_sha256_file(MANIFEST),\n        \"no_parameter_training\":True,\n        \"historical_outcome_labels_exposed\":True})\n    by_domain={}\n    for domain in DOMAINS:\n        source=g8._pack(domain)\n        models,origin=g8._load_models(\n            domain,{\"model_and_role_provenance\":manifest[\"model_and_role_provenance\"]},\n            device_name)\n        by_domain[domain]={}\n        for role in ROLES[domain]:\n            by_domain[domain][role]=score_role(\n                models,source[\"data\"],source[\"rows\"][role],origin)\n        del models\n        if torch.cuda.is_available():torch.cuda.empty_cache()\n    result=_write(RESULT,{\n        \"protocol\":PROTOCOL,\"status\":\"FROZEN_T06_ACTION_AND_RANK_DIAGNOSIS\",\n        \"by_domain\":by_domain,\n        \"manifest_file_sha256\":_sha256_file(MANIFEST),\n        \"lock_file_sha256\":_sha256_file(LOCK),\n        \"lock_self_sha256\":locked[\"result_sha256\"],\n        \"no_original_network_updates\":True,\n        \"no_train_calibration_or_confirm_fit\":True,\n        \"official_test_opened\":False,\n        \"historical_confirmation_labels_already_seen\":True,\n    })\n    REPORT.write_text(_report(result),encoding=\"utf-8\",newline=\"\\n\")\n    return {\"status\":result[\"status\"],\"result_sha256\":result[\"result_sha256\"],\n            \"mean_minus_median_by_domain\":{\n                domain:{role:{\n                    key:value[\"mean_delta_mae_m\"]\n                    for key,value in by_domain[domain][role][\"decision_effects\"].items()}\n                    for role in by_domain[domain]} for domain in DOMAINS}}\n\n\ndef check()->dict:\n    if not MANIFEST.exists():return {\"status\":\"UNPREPARED\"}\n    prepare()\n    if not LOCK.exists():return {\"status\":\"PLAN_FROZEN\"}\n    lock=_read(LOCK)\n    if lock[\"manifest_file_sha256\"]!=_sha256_file(MANIFEST):\n        raise G12Error(\"lock manifest mismatch\")\n    if not RESULT.exists():return {\"status\":\"LOCK_WITHOUT_RESULT_STOP\"}\n    result=_read(RESULT)\n    if (result[\"lock_file_sha256\"]!=_sha256_file(LOCK)\n        or result[\"lock_self_sha256\"]!=lock[\"result_sha256\"]\n        or result[\"manifest_file_sha256\"]!=_sha256_file(MANIFEST)):\n        raise G12Error(\"result file provenance mismatch\")\n    if not REPORT.exists() or REPORT.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")!=_report(result):\n        raise G12Error(\"G12 report mismatch\")\n    return {\"status\":\"VERIFIED\",\"result_sha256\":result[\"result_sha256\"]}\n\n\ndef main(argv:Sequence[str]|None=None)->int:\n    p=argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    sub=p.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\",required=True)\n    for command in (\"preflight\",\"prepare\",\"run\",\"check\"):\n        cmd=sub.add_parser(command)\n        if command==\"run\":cmd.add_argument(\"--device\",default=\"cuda\")\n    cmd=p.parse_args(argv)\n    v=preflight() if cmd.command==\"preflight\" else (\n        prepare() if cmd.command==\"prepare\" else\n        run(cmd.device) if cmd.command==\"run\" else check())\n    print(json.dumps(v,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2,allow_nan=False))\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__==\"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n"}, "tests/test_uji_v17_g12_action_ranking.py": {"sha256": "3becf787c03bd732c38058c25b685a012a3dcee1c9fee9a732819929fd871e57", "text": "\"\"\"G12 fixed-likelihood science tests: geometry, posterior invariance and rank attribution.\n\nAll tests are synthetic CPU-only; none loads historical CAL/CONFIRM outcomes.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport inspect\nimport json\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pytest\nimport torch\n\nfrom fhm_dapp_tim.fhm_dapp import uji_v17_g12_action_ranking as g12\nfrom fhm_dapp_tim.fhm_dapp.coherent_marked_v9 import (\n    common_student_t_randomness,\n)\n\n\ndef test_fixed_configuration_and_scientific_scope():\n    assert (g12.E,g12.L,g12.K)==(5,192,192)\n    assert g12.TEMPERATURE==.6\n    assert g12.ACTION_DRAWS==g12.RISK_DRAWS==128\n    assert g12.ACTION_SEED!=g12.RISK_SEED\n    assert g12.RADIUS==10.\n    assert g12.ACTIONS==(\"mean\",\"component_median\",\"continuous_median\")\n    assert g12.DOMAINS==(\"tuji\",\"uts\",\"tampere\")\n\n\ndef _simple_law():\n    torch.manual_seed(33)\n    b=2\n    p=torch.softmax(torch.randn(b,960),dim=1)\n    xy=torch.randn(b,960,2)*4\n    scale=torch.ones_like(xy)*.4\n    return p,xy,scale\n\n\ndef test_all_decisions_label_free_and_preserve_baseline_mean():\n    p,xy,scale=_simple_law()\n    rng=common_student_t_randomness(2,draws=128,degrees_freedom=4,seed=8)\n    actions=g12.actions_from_frozen_law(p,xy,scale,rng)\n    assert set(actions)==set(g12.ACTIONS)\n    assert all(a.shape==(2,2) for a in actions.values())\n    assert torch.equal(actions[\"mean\"],(p[:,:,None]*xy).sum(1))\n    assert \"target\" not in inspect.signature(g12.actions_from_frozen_law).parameters\n    assert \"true_floor\" not in inspect.signature(g12.actions_from_frozen_law).parameters\n\n\ndef test_symmetric_frozen_mixture_medians_near_mean():\n    p=torch.full((1,960),1/960)\n    points=torch.zeros(1,960,2)\n    points[:,:480,0]=-2\n    points[:,480:,0]=2\n    scale=torch.ones_like(points)*.01\n    rng=common_student_t_randomness(1,draws=128,degrees_freedom=4,seed=19)\n    a=g12.actions_from_frozen_law(p,points,scale,rng)\n    assert abs(a[\"mean\"][0,0])<1e-4\n    # A symmetric two-point median is not unique; zero is a valid minimizer.\n    assert abs(a[\"component_median\"][0,0])<.1\n    assert abs(a[\"continuous_median\"][0,1])<.2\n\n\ndef test_component_median_and_continuous_median_distinct_when_scale_matters():\n    p=torch.full((1,960),1/960)\n    point=torch.zeros((1,960,2))\n    point[:,500:,0]=10.\n    scale=torch.ones_like(point)\n    scale[:,:500]*=.01\n    scale[:,500:]*=1.\n    rng=common_student_t_randomness(1,draws=128,degrees_freedom=4,seed=14)\n    a=g12.actions_from_frozen_law(p,point,scale,rng)\n    assert all(torch.isfinite(z).all() for z in a.values())\n    # No artificially imposed equality between Dirac centre and continuous actions.\n    assert not torch.equal(a[\"component_median\"],a[\"continuous_median\"])\n\n\ndef test_independent_model_risk_evaluates_only_posterior_not_true_location():\n    p,xy,scale=_simple_law()\n    action_rng=common_student_t_randomness(2,draws=128,degrees_freedom=4,seed=23)\n    risk_rng=common_student_t_randomness(2,draws=128,degrees_freedom=4,seed=24)\n    actions=g12.actions_from_frozen_law(p,xy,scale,action_rng)\n    risk=g12.predicted_point_risk(actions,p,xy,scale,risk_rng)\n    assert set(risk)==set(g12.ACTIONS)\n    assert all(v.shape==(2,) and torch.isfinite(v).all() for v in risk.values())\n    assert \"target\" not in inspect.signature(g12.predicted_point_risk).parameters\n\n\ndef _synthetic_stage():\n    torch.manual_seed(12)\n    b=2;a=195\n    distance=torch.rand(b,a)\n    logits=torch.randn(5,b,a)\n    full=torch.softmax(logits-2*distance[None],dim=2)\n    ids=torch.arange(192)[None,None,:].expand(5,b,192).clone()\n    top=full.gather(2,ids)\n    top=top/top.sum(2,keepdim=True)\n    rad=torch.ones(5,b)\n    # Final stage can have any CONSENSUS top K; identity in this test.\n    consensus_ids=torch.arange(192)[None,:].expand(b,192).clone()\n    c=torch.softmax(torch.randn(b,192),dim=1)\n    return distance,logits,full,top,ids,rad,consensus_ids,c\n\n\ndef test_six_stage_probabilities_shapes_and_mass():\n    args=_synthetic_stage()\n    maps=g12.ranking_probability_panels(*args)\n    assert tuple(maps)==g12.STAGES\n    for name,p in maps.items():\n        assert p.shape==(2,195),name\n        assert torch.isfinite(p).all(),name\n        assert torch.all(p>=0)\n        assert torch.allclose(p.sum(1),torch.ones(2),atol=1e-6)\n\n\ndef test_fused_equal_and_radial_identical_if_member_radials_equal():\n    args=list(_synthetic_stage())\n    a=g12.ranking_probability_panels(*args)\n    assert torch.allclose(a[\"fused_equal_members\"],a[\"fused_radial_members\"],\n                          atol=1e-7)\n\n\ndef test_concentration_does_not_change_top_one():\n    p=torch.softmax(torch.randn(4,192),dim=1)\n    assert torch.equal(p.argmax(1),p.pow(1/.6).argmax(1))\n\n\ndef test_truth_only_in_retrospective_rank_diagnostic():\n    torch.manual_seed(2)\n    args=_synthetic_stage()\n    maps=g12.ranking_probability_panels(*args)\n    xy=torch.stack((torch.arange(195)*25.,torch.zeros(195)),dim=1).float()\n    building=torch.zeros(195,dtype=torch.long)\n    floor=torch.zeros(195,dtype=torch.long)\n    floor[0]=1\n    true_xy=torch.tensor([[0.,0.],[50.,0.]])\n    tb=torch.zeros(2,dtype=torch.long)\n    tf=torch.zeros(2,dtype=torch.long)\n    x=g12.ranking_label_diagnostics(maps,xy,building,floor,true_xy,tb,tf)\n    assert x[\"near_reference_exists\"].shape==(2,)\n    assert x[\"near_reference_exists\"].tolist()==[0.,1.]\n    for stage in g12.STAGES:\n        assert x[stage+\"_top1_in10m\"].shape==(2,)\n        assert x[stage+\"_near10_mass\"].shape==(2,)\n        assert x[stage+\"_best_near_rank\"].shape==(2,)\n        assert torch.isnan(x[stage+\"_best_near_rank\"][0])\n    assert \"true_xy\" not in inspect.signature(g12.ranking_probability_panels).parameters\n\n\ndef test_rank_near_mass_respects_correct_floor_even_with_same_coordinate():\n    a=192\n    p=torch.full((1,a),1/a)\n    maps={name:p for name in g12.STAGES}\n    xy=torch.zeros(a,2)\n    floor=torch.ones(a,dtype=torch.long)\n    floor[0]=0\n    valid=g12.ranking_label_diagnostics(\n        maps,xy,torch.zeros(a,dtype=torch.long),floor,\n        torch.zeros(1,2),torch.zeros(1,dtype=torch.long),\n        torch.zeros(1,dtype=torch.long))\n    assert valid[\"R3_consensus_K192_near10_mass\"].item()==pytest.approx(1/192)\n    assert valid[\"near_reference_exists\"].item()==1.\n\n\ndef test_site_macro_and_null_rank_aggregation():\n    g=torch.tensor([0,0,1,1])\n    v=torch.tensor([1.,float(\"nan\"),3.,5.])\n    assert g12._site_vector(v,g,2)==[1.,4.]\n    assert g12._site_vector(torch.full((4,),float(\"nan\")),g,2)==[None,None]\n    metrics=g12._summary({\"mean_mae_m\":[1.,3.,8.]})\n    assert metrics[\"mean_mae_m\"][\"site_mean\"]==4\n    assert metrics[\"mean_mae_m\"][\"max_m\"]==8\n\n\ndef test_input_shape_fail_closed():\n    args=list(_synthetic_stage())\n    args[3]=args[3][:,:-1,:]\n    with pytest.raises(g12.G12Error,match=\"mismatched\"):\n        g12.ranking_probability_panels(*args)\n    p,xy,scale=_simple_law()\n    with pytest.raises(g12.G12Error,match=\"invalid\"):\n        g12.actions_from_frozen_law(p,xy,scale*0,\n            common_student_t_randomness(2,draws=128))\n\n\ndef test_action_risk_not_mislabeled_energy_score():\n    text=inspect.getsource(g12)\n    assert \"shared_student_t_es_m\" in text\n    assert \"mean_model_risk_m\" in text or 'name+\"_model_risk_m\"' in text\n    assert \"g8.hierarchical_laws(joint,E,K)\" in text\n    assert '[\"anchor\"]' in text\n    assert \"g5.weighted_component_geometric_median(\" in text\n    assert \"spatial_median_from_draws(\" in text\n\n\ndef test_old_source_untouched_and_no_model_learning():\n    source=inspect.getsource(g12)\n    assert \"r2b._prototype_distance(\" in source\n    assert \"r3._member_top_l(\" in source\n    assert \"r3._dense_joint_law(\" in source\n    assert \"r3.dense_alpha_consensus_prior(\" in source\n    assert \"g8._load_models(\" in source\n    assert \"optimizer.step()\" not in source\n    assert \"train_member(\" not in source\n    assert \"official_test_opened\" in source\n\n\ndef test_frozen_result_cannot_be_overwritten(tmp_path):\n    path=tmp_path/\"frozen.json\"\n    x=g12._write(path,{\"data\":\"immutable\"})\n    assert g12._read(path)==x\n    with pytest.raises(FileExistsError):\n        g12._write(path,{\"data\":\"changed\"})\n    x[\"data\"]=\"tampered\"\n    path.write_text(json.dumps(x),encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    with pytest.raises(g12.G12Error,match=\"hash changed\"):\n        g12._read(path)\n\n\ndef test_lock_prohibits_second_run(monkeypatch,tmp_path):\n    lock=tmp_path/\"run.lock\"\n    lock.write_text(\"yes\")\n    monkeypatch.setattr(g12,\"LOCK\",lock)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(g12,\"RESULT\",tmp_path/\"none\")\n    with pytest.raises(g12.G12Error,match=\"already attempted\"):\n        g12.run(\"cpu\")\n\n\ndef test_rng_seed_and_sampling_are_frozen_for_three_domains():\n    assert (g12.ACTION_SEED,g12.RISK_SEED)==(19801,19802)\n    assert g12.PREDICTIVE_ES_SEED==g12.g8.SEED\n    assert g12.MEDIAN_ITERATIONS==64\n    assert g12.MEDIAN_TOL==1e-5\n"}}, "original_models": {"fhm_dapp_tim/models/v17_g4_observable_support/member_01_seed17301.pt": "299b5955967acc333fccef45d6a83ca45af4a6e073bf64a909ba9889dabb4fb5", "fhm_dapp_tim/models/v17_g4_observable_support/member_02_seed17302.pt": "3bf3db6c88d3189529623106af2e1463e44b17408965eeecd98a739efa8d9b48", "fhm_dapp_tim/models/v17_g4_observable_support/member_03_seed17303.pt": "4e56c499c837a40d45c9a40b984ec12eb7bc9f10dd8db5ae2b549103d05e7548", "fhm_dapp_tim/models/v17_g4_observable_support/member_04_seed17304.pt": "695b0afbc0c282f20f6f7f41d385b842b169ef366c75f0c010e5f27f24bd1224", "fhm_dapp_tim/models/v17_g4_observable_support/member_05_seed17305.pt": "0067c6a6f4d88c5dc49a9159d26304802be14e31f6cbcf23b91c29555c5ef25c", "fhm_dapp_tim/models/v17_g5_bayes_action/member_01_seed17301.pt": "8af93392f81c8cc71c7e44664da8aa3c62356f1eb8e067feff072dba3e67e60b", "fhm_dapp_tim/models/v17_g5_bayes_action/member_02_seed17302.pt": "37c8af1d611586456e6200d3fe196f111f4e93249613d4997ccdef6f9541e294", "fhm_dapp_tim/models/v17_g5_bayes_action/member_03_seed17303.pt": "c1e173049c37ef26858ada993f8d3fa62ea150ff55b7c6ccd34bd31eb0b04f2d", "fhm_dapp_tim/models/v17_g5_bayes_action/member_04_seed17304.pt": "0f53c19750169c95327f501172e2da60a690b08dcf19db677a78365b848280f1", "fhm_dapp_tim/models/v17_g5_bayes_action/member_05_seed17305.pt": "ccd93aee342b27b67b3f971f157286886d7090556bd28cdbdb4af82f350ef3b5", "fhm_dapp_tim/models/v17_g6_distribution_calibration/member_01_seed17301.pt": "20415c513976bbdd2e6aaf911c284d5a3aca271b037c41b859dce7cf89195f2a", "fhm_dapp_tim/models/v17_g6_distribution_calibration/member_02_seed17302.pt": "febeb7b185cee8b05e748616d99342f352b77d6bd0a8a0f758ad3c5a484b44e8", "fhm_dapp_tim/models/v17_g6_distribution_calibration/member_03_seed17303.pt": "73ac17a495574be6ea80989982463083ab4db58b5f87f521fed82846a53ecf0a", "fhm_dapp_tim/models/v17_g6_distribution_calibration/member_04_seed17304.pt": "58bd77a131b59dae28d9e0d513055746383f6f7edf973650fa155cc94ff7611b", "fhm_dapp_tim/models/v17_g6_distribution_calibration/member_05_seed17305.pt": "124626cbf93dd9b834a5325b61c6ff7735ed89254c9a16fae174d0a9bd79d26c"}, "protected_files": {"V